            "lens": "review-risk",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all three changed paths in full. The stem helper in engine/review/names.go keeps the strict validation CheckResultName had before: the head must be exactly 12 lowercase hex characters and the number must be canonical digits. Names containing path separators, dots or other characters are therefore still refused, so no path traversal or injection surface was added.",
              "Exemption and verdict names cannot be mistaken for results. The result reader cuts only the .json suffix, which leaves a number like '1.exempt' or '1.verifier' that canonicalNumber rejects. The new tests exercise this separation and also cover the empty-prefix and short-head cases.",
              "ExemptionsOfHead and ExemptionName are pure name functions with no I/O, no authorization decision and no secrets. An exemption file is never counted as a reviewed result by ResultsOfHead, so the change does not weaken the review gate. The change adds no dependencies."
            ]
          }
        }
