            "lens": "review-reliability",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "engine/review/names.go: the new stem helper keeps the old CheckResultName logic: cut the suffix, split at the first dash, require 12 lowercase hex characters and a canonical number. A name ending in .verifier.json or .exempt.json leaves a number such as 1.verifier or 1.exempt when cut with the .json suffix, which canonicalNumber rejects. A result reader therefore cannot take either of those files, and CheckResultName behaves as before for valid inputs.",
              "engine/review/check.go: ResultsOfHead now delegates to ofHead with resultSuffix. The prefix filter and the stem check together match the old HasPrefix plus CheckResultName test, and the sort by launch number is unchanged. ExemptionsOfHead reuses the same path with exemptionSuffix, and a short or empty head gives a prefix beginning with a dash, which no name matches.",
              "engine/review/exempt_names_test.go: the tests assert externally observable behavior at unit level. They cover ordering, exclusion of look-alike names (leading zero, temporary file, dot prefix, non-numeric, missing number, wrong head), no mutation of the input slice, cross-kind isolation, and shared numbering through NextNumber. NextNumber is unchanged and its '.'-after-number rule already counts exemption names. The tests also call VerdictName and ResultOfVerdict, which this diff does not show. They are existing behavior, and nothing visible contradicts the expectations.",
              "No defects found that this candidate introduced."
            ]
          }
        }
